{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-1","title":"Ezekiel 5:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Under the type of hair, 5 is shewn the judgment of Jerusalem for their rebellion; 12 by famine, sword, and dispersion.</p>\n<p>son.In this expressive emblem, the prophet represents the Jewish nation; his hair, the people; the razor, the Chaldeans; the cutting of the hair, the calamities and disgrace coming upon them; the balances, the exact distribution of the Divine judgments; the third part of the hair burnt, those destroyed in the city; the third part smitten with a knife, those slain in attempting to escape; the third part scattered to the winds, those who escaped to other countries; the few hairs in his skirt, those left with Gedaliah; and the burning of these, their destruction in Egypt.</p>\n<p>take. 44:20; Le 21:5; Isa 7:20 then. Da 5:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-2","title":"Ezekiel 5:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>shalt burn. 12; Jer 9:21,22; 15:2; 24:10; 38:2 the city. 4:1-8 I will draw. 12; 12:14; Le 26:33; Jer 9:16; Am 9:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-3","title":"Ezekiel 5:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>a few. 2Ki 25:12; Jer 39:10; 40:6; 52:16; Mt 7:14; Lu 13:23,24; 1Pe 4:18 skirts. Heb. wings.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-4","title":"Ezekiel 5:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>take. 2Ki 25:25; Jer 41:1-44:30; 52:30 shall a fire. Jer 4:4; 48:45</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-5","title":"Ezekiel 5:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>This. 4:1; Jer 6:6; Lu 22:19,20; 1Co 10:4 I have. 16:14; De 4:6; Mic 5:7; Mt 5:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-6","title":"Ezekiel 5:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>she hath. 16:47; De 32:15-21; 2Ki 17:8-20; Ps 106:20; Ro 1:23-25; 1Co 5:1 Jude 1:4 for they. Ne 9:16,17; Ps 78:10; Jer 5:3; 8:5; 9:6; 11:10; Zec 7:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-7","title":"Ezekiel 5:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>neither have done. 11; 16:47,48,54; 2Ki 21:9-11; 2Ch 33:9; Jer 2:10,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-8","title":"Ezekiel 5:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>even I. 15:7; 21:3; 26:3; 28:22; 35:3; 39:1; Le 26:17-46; De 29:20 Jer 21:5,13; La 2:5; 3:3; Zec 14:2,3; Mt 22:7 in the. 25:2-6; 26:2; 29:6,7; 35:10-15; De 29:23-28; 1Ki 9:8,9; Jer 22:8,9 Jer 24:9; 50:7; La 2:15-17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-9","title":"Ezekiel 5:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>that which. La 4:6,9; Da 9:12; Am 3:2; Mt 24:21 The sentence here passed upon Jerusalem is very dreadful, and the manner of expression makes it yet more so: the judgments are various, the threatenings of them varied, reiterated; so that one may well say, Who is able to stand in God's sight when he is angry?</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-10","title":"Ezekiel 5:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>the fathers. Le 26:29; De 28:53-57,64; 2Ki 6:29; Isa 9:20; 49:26; Jer 19:9 La 2:20; 4:10 the whole. 2,12; 6:8; 12:14; 20:23; 22:15; 36:19; Le 26:33; De 4:27; 28:64 De 32:26; Ne 1:8; Ps 44:11; Jer 9:16; 44:12; 50:17; Am 9:9; Zec 2:6 Zec 7:14; Lu 21:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-11","title":"Ezekiel 5:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>as I live. Nu 14:28-35; Ps 95:11; Am 8:7; Heb 6:13 thou hast. 8:5,6,16; 23:28; 44:7; 2Ki 21:4,7; 23:12; 2Ch 33:4,7; 36:14 Jer 7:9-11; 32:34 detestable. 7:20; 11:18,21; De 7:25,26; Jer 16:18; 44:4 will I. 29:15; Ps 107:39; Jer 10:24; *marg: Ro 11:12 neither shall. 7:4,9; 8:18; 9:5,10; 24:14; De 29:20; La 2:21; Zec 11:6; Mal 3:17 Ro 8:32; 11:21; 2Pe 2:4,5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-12","title":"Ezekiel 5:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>third part of. 2; 6:12; Jer 15:2; 21:9; Zec 13:7-9 and I will scatter. 2,10; 6:8; Jer 9:16; Zec 7:14 and I will draw.This was particularly fulfilled in the destruction of those who retired to Egypt; and has been remarkably verified in the many persecutions and miseries which the Jews have suffered at different times, in the various countries into which they are dispersed.</p>\n<p>2; 12:14; Le 26:33; De 28:65; Jer 42:16,17,22; 43:10,11; 44:27 Am 9:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-13","title":"Ezekiel 5:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>shall mine. 6:12; 7:8; 13:15; 20:8,21; Jer 25:12; La 4:11,22; Da 9:2; 11:36 I will cause. 16:42,63; 21:17; 23:25; 24:13; Isa 1:21 I will be. De 32:36; Isa 1:24; Zec 6:8 spoken. 6:10; 36:5,6; 38:18,19; Isa 9:7; 59:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-14","title":"Ezekiel 5:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>I will. 22:4; Le 26:31,32; De 28:37; 2Ch 7:20,21; Ne 2:17; Ps 74:3-10 Ps 79:1-4; Isa 64:10,11; Jer 19:8; 24:9,10; 42:18; La 1:4,8 La 2:15-17; 5:18; Mic 3:12 the nations. 8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-15","title":"Ezekiel 5:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>an instruction. De 29:24-28; 1Ki 9:7; Ps 79:4; Isa 26:9; Jer 22:8,9; 1Co 10:11 when. 25:17; Isa 66:15,16; Na 1:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-16","title":"Ezekiel 5:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>the evil. De 32:23,24; Ps 7:13; 91:5-7; La 3:12 and will. 4:16; 14:13; Le 26:26; 2Ki 6:25; Isa 3:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-5-17","title":"Ezekiel 5:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>and evil. 14:15,21; 33:27; 34:25-28; Ex 23:29; Le 26:22; De 32:24; 2Ki 17:25 Jer 15:3 and pestilence. 12; 14:19; 38:22 and I. 6:12; 21:3; 23:47 I the. 13,15; 17:21,24; 21:32; 22:14; 26:14; 30:12; 37:14; Mt 24:35</p>"}]}